---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title="About">
  <section class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT DRAKELABS</p><h1>Curiosity,<br /><em>with a workbench.</em></h1><p class="lead">DrakeLabs is my home for building, running, and understanding technology — and for sharing the work that makes it all fit together.</p></section>
  <section class="section two-col" aria-labelledby="origin-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">HOW IT STARTED</p><h2 id="origin-heading">It started with streaming fatigue.</h2><p>I hadn’t planned on building a project this big. I was tired of paying for multiple streaming services and wanted to collect and organize my own media for myself and my family.</p><p>I wanted a library we could keep, without a streaming service deciding to remove a favorite show or movie. One familiar interface for everything, with control over the environment behind it.</p></div><div><p class="eyebrow">WHY DOCUMENT IT</p><h2>A bigger project.<br />A lot of learning.</h2><p>As the setup grew, so did the work involved in making it all fit together. What began as a practical family project became a place to learn by building and running real systems. I started with very little Linux experience; Ubuntu became my OS of choice, and along the way I became confident working in the command line.</p><p>DrakeLabs is a way to document that work for myself and showcase what I’ve learned: the choices, the troubleshooting, and the improvements along the way.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}infrastructure/#guiding-goals`}>Explore the goals behind the lab →</a></div></section>
  <section class="section two-col"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE APPROACH</p><h2>Make the learning visible.</h2><p>A useful portfolio should show more than a finished screen. It should explain the question, the constraints, and the choices behind the result.</p><p>This site starts with a family media system and grows from there. The aim is a record of practical work, with enough context to be useful to someone else.</p></div><div class="manifesto"><span>01 / BUILD WITH INTENT</span><h3>Understand the pieces.</h3><span>02 / DOCUMENT THE CHOICES</span><h3>Keep the reasoning.</h3><span>03 / KEEP ITERATING</span><h3>Leave room to improve.</h3></div></section>
  <section class="note-strip"><p class="eyebrow">BUILDING IN THE OPEN</p><h2>Show the process, too.</h2><p>The earlier lab was built and configured by me, with AI helping with research and Bash and Python scripts that I manually reviewed. Direct implementation by AI agents is a recent addition to the process, including this website.</p><p>I want readers to see both the progress and how the work was done — and eventually have a straightforward, tested path to build their own version.</p><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href={`${base}journal/#timeline`}>Follow the timeline →</a><a class="text-link" href={`${base}infrastructure/#build-your-own`}>Explore the guide roadmap →</a></div></section>
  <section class="note-strip"><p class="eyebrow">WHAT COMES NEXT</p><h2>A home for the work.</h2><p>DrakeLabs lives at drakelabs.org, with website source and future project repositories in the DrakeLabs GitHub organization. The portfolio and service status page are hosted independently of the home lab.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}projects/`}>Explore the work →</a></section>
</Layout>
